WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.820
- Did you get, I'm asking everyone,

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:04.360
did you get the same gift
from Tom Hanks at the end?

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.193
- Okay, listen.

00:00:05.193 --> 00:00:06.336
I was so happy you didn't
know what it was either.

00:00:06.336 --> 00:00:07.169
- No!

00:00:08.544 --> 00:00:10.040
- 'Cause I was strugglin'.
- But I love that this is

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.310
coming out here.
- Here.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.463
On a public forum.

00:00:12.463 --> 00:00:13.470
- I know!
- My favorite!

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.590
- How dare we not know
- I know!

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.960
- what Sir Tom Hanks gave us as a gift!

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.290
It's our fault.
- I know!

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:19.690
- It's our fault, actually.
- It's so funny!

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.760
- It's either a riding,

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.458
like something to ride
a horse, or something--

00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:26.590
(laughing boisterously)

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:29.457
- I am so excited about the guesses!

00:00:29.457 --> 00:00:30.691
- Yes, it is the equestrian's companion.

00:00:30.691 --> 00:00:31.524
- It is!

00:00:31.524 --> 00:00:33.133
- Yes.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.020
I realize now.
- Or you put a paper in it.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:35.853
I don't know!

00:00:35.853 --> 00:00:36.905
It's one or the other.

00:00:36.905 --> 00:00:38.020
- I think it's more like
loose-leafed papers.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.405
- This is just--
- Or tobacco.

00:00:40.405 --> 00:00:42.304
(laughing)

00:00:42.304 --> 00:00:45.950
- This is the greatest
quest I've ever been on.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.350
Matthew and Susan were both telling us

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.581
that you gave the most awesome wrap gift.

00:00:50.581 --> 00:00:52.407
They were like, "It's so beautiful!

00:00:52.407 --> 00:00:53.240
"It's leather.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.432
"It's inscribed.

00:00:54.432 --> 00:00:55.265
"It's so beautiful."

00:00:55.265 --> 00:00:56.098
- It's got the name on it, yeah.

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:58.003
- Yes, and they were like, we
just don't know what it is!

00:00:58.003 --> 00:00:59.390
- Know what it is.

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.311
(laughing)

00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:03.760
- And you're Tom Hanks so
they were too afraid to ask!

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.260
- Here's what it is.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.750
When you show up to work on a movie,

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.120
you have a copy of the
pages that you're...

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:10.953
They're called sides--

00:01:10.953 --> 00:01:11.786
- Sides, yeah.

00:01:11.786 --> 00:01:13.500
- The script pages that
you're shooting that day,

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.333
and the call sheet,

00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:16.800
so everybody knows
exactly what you're doing.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.246
They are leather holders for those sides.

00:01:19.246 --> 00:01:20.440
And there's a little pen,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.047
and you can keep notes on it.
- That's very thoughtful!

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:25.500
- I've used it on complicated days,

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.730
'cause you need to know.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.980
And the fact that neither Susan

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.670
nor Matthew knew what they were--

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:32.575
- No, but the fact that there were two--

00:01:32.575 --> 00:01:33.699
- Are these people professional actors?

00:01:33.699 --> 00:01:34.907
I don't understand.
- No, no!

00:01:34.907 --> 00:01:36.970
It's because they were like,
it's so beautiful, but...

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:38.037
She even said, "I don't know.

00:01:38.037 --> 00:01:39.240
"Some sort of saddle." (laughing)

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.114
I don't know what she said.

00:01:41.114 --> 00:01:42.340
- Use it as a coin purse!

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:43.257
I don't care!

00:01:43.257 --> 00:01:44.360
- But it was funny though,

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.410
because then they're gonna
figure it out though.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.380
And it makes perfect sense.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.480
It's the most perfect wrap gift.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.313
- It's a tool.
- It's beautiful.

00:01:49.313 --> 00:01:50.146
Now they know.

00:01:50.146 --> 00:01:52.120
- Now they know.
- The more you know.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.840
- So, take it down from the shelf,

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.620
take it out of its shrink wrap,

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.267
and use the damn things,
for cryin' out loud.

